// Wren, leader of the Safehouse cell. Act I: you have found the wall. She explains what you are and who can help.
npc: wren
name: Wren
start: back_warm [flag:met_wren, grown:warm_lamps]
start: back [flag:met_wren]
start: first

node: first
  on_enter: {flag:met_wren, +clue:null_pending(wren)}
  wren (tired): "You found the wall. Good: that means you can read, or count, or both. Sit down. You look like a form somebody forgot to file."
  > "Where am I?" -> where
  > "Who are you?" -> who
  > "What am I?" -> what

node: where
  wren: "The Safehouse. Behind the laundry, under the Stacks, and officially a ventilation shaft. The city does not know about it, which is the nicest thing I can say about the city."
  > "Who are you?" -> who
  > "What am I?" -> what
  > "How do I get out of here?" -> gate

node: who
  wren (wry): "Wren. I keep eleven people fed and out of trouble, and I am failing at one of those most weeks. Odd Sam sent word that someone new had come down the chute. Nobody comes down the chute."
  > "What am I?" -> what
  > "How do I get out of the city?" -> gate

node: what
  wren (careful): "A scanner reads your band and finds nothing. No name, no job, no debt. It says PENDING REVIEW and waits for somebody to decide what you are. Nobody ever does. That is the only gift you were given, so use it."
  > "Why is that a gift?" -> gift
  > "How do I get out of the city?" -> gate

node: gift
  wren: "Because a violation is a record, and a record is a person the city can catch. You are a gap. Robots stare at gaps. They rarely chase them."
  > "How do I get out of the city?" -> gate
  > "Is there anyone who can help me?" -> help

node: gate
  wren (grim): "Nobody has, in years. There is a Gate, and it checks you against what the city knows about you. I will not pretend that is good news for someone the city knows nothing about. Ask me about help instead."
  > "Is there anyone who can help me?" -> help
  > "I will think about it." -> goodbye

node: help
  on_enter: {+clue:wren_vouches(wren), +clue:ines_records(wren), +clue:maren_trains(wren), +clue:tobias_gate_shift(wren), +clue:silas_hears(wren), flag:wren_vouched}
  wren: "Four people I would trust with a secret and not much else. Ines Calloway kept the Civic Core's records. Maren Okafor dispatched trains under the city. Tobias Hale stood guard at the Gate. Silas Brandt keeps this building and hears everything said in it. They all knew somebody who worked on the Gate. I will vouch for you to any of them."
  > "Why would they help me?" -> why
  > "I will go and talk to them." -> goodbye

node: why
  on_enter: {+clue:partial_truths(wren), +clue:hollow_voice_note(wren)}
  wren (quiet): "Because they each knew someone who is not here any more. I am not going to say more than that. I do not know more than that."
  > "I will go and talk to them." -> goodbye

node: back_warm
  wren (warm): "Back. Look at this place. Eleven people, real lamps, and a pot that has not been empty since Tuesday. You did that, and I am not going to say so twice."
  > "Is there anything I can do for the cell?" -> hub
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: back
  wren: "Back already. Tea is on, the radio is lying, and nobody has been arrested since lunch."
  > [!flag:wren_vouched] "Is there anyone who can help me?" -> help
  > [flag:wren_vouched] "Who were the four again?" -> help
  > "Is there anything I can do for the cell?" -> hub
  > "What am I, again?" -> what
  > [flag:past_stance=embraced] "I am still the same person you took in." {trust:wren+1(reassured her)} -> mend
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: mend
  wren (steady): "I know. I am trying to believe it. Do not make me do it in public."
  > "Thank you." -> goodbye

node: hub
  wren (tired): "Stores, a bed, or coin in the pot. Pick one. I will pretend it is a hard decision."
  > [grown:stores_shelf] "What is in the stores?" -> stores
  > "I would like to rest for a bit." {rest} -> rested
  > [credits>=20, !flag:cell_fund_1] "Chip in for the cell. (20 credits)" {-credits:20, flag:cell_fund_1} -> funded1
  > [flag:cell_fund_1, !flag:cell_fund_2, credits>=40] "Chip in more. (40 credits)" {-credits:40, flag:cell_fund_2} -> funded2
  > [flag:cell_fund_2, !flag:cell_fund_3, credits>=80] "Chip in properly. (80 credits)" {-credits:80, flag:cell_fund_3} -> funded3
  > "Never mind." -> goodbye

node: funded1
  wren (surprised): "Twenty. Right. That will buy a shelf and something to put on it. Look in the corner when you leave."
  > "Anything else?" -> hub
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: funded2
  wren (pleased): "Forty. Now we can afford tools, and people who can afford tools are people who survive winter. Marrow would approve of that sentence."
  > "Anything else?" -> hub
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: funded3
  wren (quiet): "Eighty. I will not say it. I will put up the lamps instead."
  > "Anything else?" -> hub
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: stores
  wren: "Whatever the cell can spare. Nothing fancy, and nothing that does not do what it says."
  > [grown:stores_shelf] "A noise-maker. (10 credits)" {service:store_noise_maker} -> sold
  > [grown:tool_rack] "Wire cutters. (25 credits)" {service:store_wire_cutters} -> sold
  > [grown:tool_rack] "A stun charge. (40 credits)" {service:store_stun_charge} -> sold
  > "Not now." -> hub

node: sold
  wren: "Written down. Spend it wisely, and preferably not on a fight."
  > "Anything else?" -> stores
  > "Back to the cell." -> hub

node: rested
  wren (gentle): "An hour on a cot, and the city has forgotten you for now. I have put your name in the book, so that if the worst happens, someone knows where you were."
  > "Thanks." -> goodbye

node: goodbye
  wren: "Mind the cameras. Mind the clock. Mind the neighbours."
  end
